/*
 * Declares the ScalarType class.
 *
 * A ScalarType represents any native type that behaves as an indivisible value.
 * Scalar types cannot be decomposed into smaller semantic components, even if
 * their runtime representation may contain multiple fields. For example,
 * delegates internally store both a function pointer and an environment
 * pointer, but semantically they behave as a single atomic value and are
 * therefore considered scalar.
 *
 * Scalar types include integers, floats, characters, booleans, function
 * pointers, delegates, `none`, `void`, and other primitive built-ins.
 *
 * ScalarType provides the shared behavior for all such types, including
 * mutability rules, addressability, and compatibility checks.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::type::native::scalar
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/type/native/scalar.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2021-11-26
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
